# HireMatch.AI

An AI-powered resume screener that scores your match against any job description, identifies missing keywords, rewrites your bullet points, generates tailored cover letters, and tracks every application in one dashboard.

**Live:** (https://hirematch-ai-six.vercel.app)

---

## Features

- **Match Score** — Resume scored against the JD (0–100%)
- **Keyword Gap Analysis** — See what ATS systems are filtering you on
- **Skill Alignment** — Visual breakdown per skill category
- **Resume Rewriter** — Bullet points rewritten for the specific job
- **Cover Letter Generator** — Tailored to both resume and JD
- **Application Tracker** — Every analysis saved with status tracking
- **Job Search Intelligence** — Patterns across all your applications

## Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|-------|------------|
| Frontend | HTML, CSS, Vanilla JavaScript |
| AI | Google Gemini 2.0 Flash |
| Backend | Vercel Serverless Functions |
| Database & Auth | Supabase |
| PDF Parsing | PDF.js |
| Deployment | Vercel |

## Setup

### 1. Clone the repo
```bash
git clone https://github.com/Nion9/hirematch-ai.git
```

### 2. Configure Supabase
1. Create a project at [supabase.com](https://supabase.com)
2. Run `supabase-setup.sql` in the SQL Editor
3. Copy your Project URL and anon key into all 3 HTML files

### 3. Get a Gemini API key
1. Get a free key at [aistudio.google.com](https://aistudio.google.com)

### 4. Deploy
1. Push to GitHub
2. Import into Vercel
3. Add `GEMINI_API_KEY` to environment variables
4. Deploy

## Project Structure

```
hirematch-ai/
├── api/
│   └── analyze.js
├── index.html
├── app.html
├── tracker.html
├── supabase-setup.sql
└── README.md
```

## Security

- Supabase Row Level Security ensures users only access their own data
- Gemini API key stored as a server-side environment variable
- PDF parsing runs entirely in the browser

